{
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "strings": {
    "birthday-plan.instructions": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ask for the date range, number of guests and kind of celebration. Find two possible slots in the family Google Calendar. In the Gmail thread I choose, collect the availability people have shared and the outstanding replies.\n\nCompare the dates and recommend the one that suits the most respondents. List tasks for a week before and the day before, then draft a short invitation showing which details are still open. Keep the draft in Vellem without sending invitations or creating an event."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Demande-moi la période, le nombre de personnes et le type de fête. Repère deux créneaux dans le Google Calendar familial. Dans le fil Gmail que je choisis, relève les disponibilités déjà exprimées et les réponses en attente.\n\nCompare les deux dates et recommande celle qui convient au plus de personnes ayant répondu. Prépare les tâches à J−7 et la veille, puis un court brouillon d’invitation avec les détails à confirmer. Garde le brouillon dans Vellem, sans envoyer d’invitation ni créer d’événement."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "birthday-plan.summary": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Possible dates, guest replies and a preparation checklist."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les créneaux possibles, les réponses des invités et les préparatifs à répartir."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "birthday-plan.title": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Organize a family birthday"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Préparer un anniversaire en famille"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "campaign-brief.instructions": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Use the Granola kickoff notes and the campaign plan in Notion for the campaign I name. If several campaigns match, ask which one to use.\n\nDraft a one-page brief with the target audience, their problem, the promise, the evidence behind it, the channels and the launch date. Close with the success metric and any decisions still needed. If the meeting and the plan disagree, quote both positions."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Croise les notes de la réunion de lancement dans Granola avec le plan Notion de la campagne que je nomme. Si plusieurs campagnes correspondent, demande-moi laquelle utiliser.\n\nRédige un brief d’une page avec le public visé, son problème, la promesse, les preuves disponibles, les canaux et la date de lancement. Termine par l’indicateur de succès et les décisions en suspens. Si le plan et la réunion se contredisent, cite les deux versions."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "campaign-brief.summary": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Turn the kickoff discussion and the launch plan into a brief for the team."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Le brief de l’équipe à partir de la réunion de lancement et du plan de campagne."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "campaign-brief.title": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Draft a campaign brief"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Préparer un brief de campagne"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "claim-check.instructions": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ask for the claim, screenshot or link I want checked. Isolate the exact statement. Trace it to the earliest identifiable source and check the date, location and context. Look for independent evidence that supports or contradicts it.\n\nGive a short verdict. Say what is established, what remains uncertain and what would change your conclusion. If the quote comes from a screenshot or clip, include the surrounding passage."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Demande-moi la phrase, la capture ou le lien à vérifier. Isole l’affirmation exacte. Retrouve sa première source identifiable et vérifie la date, le lieu et le contexte. Cherche un élément indépendant qui la confirme ou la contredit.\n\nRends un verdict court. Indique ce qui est établi, ce qui reste incertain et le détail qui pourrait changer ta conclusion. Si la citation vient d’une image ou d’un extrait, donne aussi le passage qui l’entoure."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "claim-check.summary": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Find the original source, recover the context and see what the evidence supports."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "La source d’origine, le contexte et ce que les preuves permettent de conclure."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "claim-check.title": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Check a claim that’s going around"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Vérifier une affirmation qui circule"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "client-thread.instructions": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Start with the Gmail thread I give you. Find Slack discussions that mention this customer and this request. If I haven’t provided a thread or named a customer, ask which one to use.\n\nSummarize the latest request, the commitments we’ve made and what the team has since confirmed. Finish with a draft reply to the customer. Send the draft to Vellem and leave the Gmail thread as it is."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "À partir du fil Gmail que je t’indique, retrouve les échanges Slack qui citent ce client et cette demande. Si je n’ai pas donné de fil ni de client, demande-moi lequel traiter.\n\nRésume la dernière demande, les engagements déjà communiqués et ce que l’équipe a confirmé depuis. Termine par un brouillon de réponse au client. Dépose ce brouillon dans Vellem et laisse le fil Gmail intact."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "client-thread.summary": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The customer’s email and the answers the team has already found."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "La demande par e-mail et les réponses déjà trouvées en interne."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "client-thread.title": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pick up a customer conversation"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Reprendre un échange client"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "conflicting-reports.instructions": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ask for both articles or excerpts. For each disagreement, trace it to the figures, testimony or documents cited. Check whether the accounts cover the same time period, place and population. Identify sources they share.\n\nSet the disagreements side by side. For each one, explain whether the difference comes from the data, definitions or interpretation. End with the question the sources leave open."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Demande-moi les deux articles ou leurs extraits. Pour chaque point de désaccord, remonte aux chiffres, témoignages ou documents cités. Vérifie si les deux textes parlent de la même période, du même territoire et de la même population. Repère aussi les sources qu’ils ont en commun.\n\nPrésente les divergences côte à côte. Pour chacune, explique si l’écart vient des données, de la définition ou de l’interprétation. Termine par la question que ces sources laissent ouverte."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "conflicting-reports.summary": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Find the common ground, comparable figures and the reason the accounts diverge."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les points d’accord, les chiffres comparables et l’origine du désaccord."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "conflicting-reports.title": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Compare two conflicting articles"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Comparer deux articles qui se contredisent"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "deadline-review.instructions": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Find my open Linear tickets due in the next seven days. Compare their deadlines with time off and existing commitments in my Google Calendar.\n\nList tickets by due date with their status, reported blockers and free time before the deadline during my known working hours. Say when the remaining effort is unknown. End with the first decision I need to make and the facts behind it."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Relève dans Linear mes tickets ouverts dont l’échéance tombe dans les sept prochains jours. Compare leurs dates aux absences et aux plages déjà occupées dans mon Google Calendar.\n\nPrésente les tickets par date, avec leur état, les blocages signalés et les créneaux encore libres avant l’échéance pendant mes heures de travail connues. Si l’effort restant est inconnu, indique-le. Termine par le premier arbitrage à faire, en expliquant sur quels faits il repose."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "deadline-review.summary": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Compare this week’s tickets with the time available."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les tickets à rendre cette semaine face au temps disponible."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "deadline-review.title": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Spot deadlines at risk"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Repérer les échéances à risque"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "delivery": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Send the result to Vellem in Markdown using the send_output MCP tool. Give it a title that names the subject and set folder_name to “%@”. Confirm once Vellem accepts it."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Envoie le résultat en Markdown dans Vellem avec l’outil MCP send_output. Utilise un titre qui nomme le sujet et le paramètre folder_name « %@ ». Confirme l’envoi une fois que Vellem l’a accepté."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "design-review.instructions": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Use the Notion spec and related Linear issues for the feature I name. If the feature is unclear, ask which one to review.\n\nPrepare an agenda for the design review. For each user flow, identify the states the spec covers and any gaps in empty, loading or error states. Separate decisions already made from questions that need an answer, and link each question to its source."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pars de la spec Notion et des tickets Linear de la fonctionnalité que je t’indique. Si elle n’est pas identifiée, demande-moi laquelle examiner.\n\nPrépare l’ordre du jour de la revue de design. Pour chaque parcours, relève les états décrits et les éventuels oublis concernant le chargement, les erreurs et les écrans vides. Distingue les décisions déjà prises des questions à trancher et relie chaque question à sa source."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "design-review.summary": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The flows to review, the states to check and the decisions still open."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Les parcours à relire, les états à vérifier et les décisions à prendre."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "design-review.title": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Prepare a design review"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Préparer une revue de design"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "family-outing.instructions": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ask where we are starting, the ages, budget and maximum travel time. Find a free slot in the family Google Calendar I specify. Check venue websites for opening times on that date, admission for the whole family and booking requirements.\n\nSuggest three different outings, including one indoors. Give a departure time, time on site and estimated total cost for each. Pick the best fit for our constraints and explain why in one sentence."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Demande-moi le point de départ, les âges, le budget et le trajet maximal. Repère un créneau libre dans le Google Calendar familial que je t’indique. Sur les sites des lieux, vérifie les horaires pour la date précise, les tarifs pour toute la famille et la réservation éventuelle.\n\nPropose trois sorties contrastées, dont une à l’abri. Pour chacune, donne l’heure de départ, le temps sur place et le coût total estimé. Choisis celle qui convient le mieux à nos contraintes et explique pourquoi en une phrase."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "family-outing.summary": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Three outings that fit the time available, including a rainy-day option."
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Trois idées qui tiennent dans le créneau disponible, avec une option en cas de pluie."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "family-outing.title": {
      "extractionState": "manual",
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Find a family outing for the weekend"
          }
        },
        "fr": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Trouver une sortie pour ce week-end"
          }
        }
      }
    },
